{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "d8fdf96d-0c2d-8ea0-ac81-d591f3f21e90",
  "created_at": "2026-01-25T10:48:56-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Public Works",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Elvis Andrade",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Denise Arruda",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-25T10:46:29-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Public Works storm line, this is Denise."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-25T10:46:32-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hello. Yes. My name is Elvis Andrade. I call about the snow. The plow."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-25T10:46:38-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, Mr. Andrade. Which street are you on?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-25T10:46:42-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Ninety-five Dixon Street. North End. It is dead end. The street, it is dead end."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-25T10:46:48-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Dixon Street, got it. Has the plow been through yet?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-25T10:46:52-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No. Not yet. Always the same. The dead end, they come last. Always last. Every storm, last."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-25T10:46:59-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I hear you. Dead-end streets do tend to get done after the main roads. Is it still snowing there?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-25T10:47:07-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Now it is changing to rain. Wet, heavy snow. Very heavy. I cannot take the car out. Is Sunday, and I call the storm line because City Hall is closed, yes? I think nobody is there."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-25T10:47:20-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Right, the main offices are closed on Sunday, but this line is staffed during the storm. You called the right place."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-25T10:47:28-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. Good. Sorry, one moment. [pause] I am at my work, in the break room. Somebody make popcorn, the smell is very strong. Sorry."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-25T10:47:37-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No, that's fine. So you're not home right now?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-25T10:47:41-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No, I am at work. But my wife, she is home. She says the street has nothing. No plow. And now the rain, it will freeze tonight. I am worried, no, I am angry. Every time, same."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-25T10:47:55-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Understood. I'll note Dixon Street as a dead end that hasn't been plowed. Is there something else you need?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-25T10:48:02-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes. Please, sand. Can you send sand to my street? For the ice. Nobody can walk. The hill at the end, it is bad."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-25T10:48:11-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I'll put in a request for sand along with the plow. I can't tell you exactly when the truck gets there, because crews are working through the whole city today. But it's logged."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-25T10:48:23-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Logged. Okay. But when? Tonight? Tomorrow morning?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-25T10:48:26-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I really can't give you a time. With the rain coming, they'll be prioritizing the main roads first, then the side streets. If it's still not done by tomorrow morning, call back and we'll follow up."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-25T10:48:39-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. I call tomorrow. This number is good, 401-555-0187. If they need."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-25T10:48:44-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Got it, 401-555-0187. I've got your request for 95 Dixon Street."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-25T10:48:49-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Thank you. Please, do not forget the dead end."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-25T10:48:53-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I won't. Take care, Mr. Andrade."
    }
  ],
